186332900 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $P(5,3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332900 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1406bce6-76e7-5954-aca6-0e4b86d8b417" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332900 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\n$P(5,3)$ means the same thing as ${}_{5}{P}_{3}.$ Using the usual formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5,3) & =\\frac{5!}{(5-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5!}{2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{2!}}{\\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332932 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186332262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332932 #edb/ref 1069 "q-5563" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332932 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332932 #edb/ref 1071 "${}_{6}{P}_{1}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332932 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "03be0042-eceb-55bb-8772-451be81dc234" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332932 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=6$ and $r=1$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{6}{P}_{1} & =\\frac{6!}{(6-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6!}{5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351585 #edb/ref 1080 "14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351585 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351585 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "025397b0-bbd9-5ef2-a77e-3a61df4ea918" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352199 #edb/ref 1080 "16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352199 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352199 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "44a461b1-5ca1-51c8-9f74-db33ed70426e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352710 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352710 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186