 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $4$ cards, so $n=4.$ We want to select $2$ of those cards to make a sequence of $2$ cards, so we have $r=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to choose the cards is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{4}{P}_{2} & =\\frac{4!}{(4-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4!}{2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{2!}}{\\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394621 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394621 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394621 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394621 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394621 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394621 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394621 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394621 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186394623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394621 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "72d9fa78-c6ea-5ff0-a6cb-0b7ec2cbcfc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394622 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\,016" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394622 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394622 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aaed84db-333e-5211-84c5-2d24c1d90316" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394623 #edb/ref 1080 "3\\,024" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394623 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394623 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e1c1b16c-2ec4-5950-92f8-59f867978e1e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394624 #edb/ref 1080 "120" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394624 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394624 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "542940cc-ac17-5702-9c22-d185b7bb47c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921863